snippet.description:
While on the Alabama Coast, the weather finally cleared on Sunday morning. On the shoreline of Lake Shelby (or Shelby Lake) in Gulf State Park, US-1042, I was finally able to activate from outside of the truck cab.
I put up the vertical and Buddy coil to start on 40m.  The system tuned up to 1.05:1 and I was off to the races.  Thankfully, both 40m and 20m cooperated and I enjoyed a great time on the picnic table.  One of the hi-lights was a great DX contact in the Cayman Islands!  Thanks PHIL.
